SUMMARY:NEW TRAIL! 🍂 From Scarborough to North York: The Fall Colours T
 rail Walk 🌈
DESCRIPTION:Try New Things in Toronto!\n# 🍂 From Scarborough to North Y
 ork: The Fall Colours Trail Walk 🌈\n\n### A Scenic Fall Adventure Throu
 gh Trails\, Ravines & Toronto History\n\nToronto has some wonderful natura
 l spaces tucked between its neighbourhoods\, and this walk connects two of
  them into one longer adventure!\n\nWe’ll begin in Scarborough\, explori
 ng the **Gatineau Corridor Trail**\, with its wildflowers\, tall grasses\,
  and green spaces where nature is allowed to grow a little more freely. 
 🍁 From there\, we’ll make our way along some city streets before conn
 ecting with another trail system and continuing through the surrounding ra
 vines toward the **Rainbow Tunnel**.\n\nThe tunnel is an unusual piece of 
 Toronto history\, painted in 1971 by teenager B.C. Johnson as a tribute to
  his friend Sigred\, who died in a car accident. Although the artwork has 
 seen better days\, we’ll make a quick stop to see it before continuing t
 oward our final destination.\n\nWe’ll finish at **Shops at Don Mills**\,
  where anyone who wants to can join us for coffee\, a pastry\, or somethin
 g to eat after the walk. ☕🥐\nThis is a longer outing than some of our
  regular walks\, but we’ll take our time\, enjoy the scenery\, and have 
 a break along the way.\n\n***\n\n### 🚶‍♂️ What We’ll Do\n\nAlon
 g the route\, we’ll:\n\n* Explore the Gatineau Corridor Trail and its na
 turalized green spaces 🌼\n* Walk through parks and neighbourhood street
 s\n* Take a break midway through the walk\n* Connect with the Moccasin Tra
 il and surrounding ravine paths 🌳\n* Stop briefly at the Rainbow Tunnel
  🌈\n* Continue to Shops at Don Mills\n* Finish with an optional coffee 
 or snack with the group ☕\n\nThe walk should take approximately **3 hour
 s**\, depending on the pace of the group and the conditions along the rout
 e.\n**Please note:** This is a point-to-point walk. We will not return to 
 our starting location at Dollar Tree. At the end\, I’ll help anyone who 
 needs assistance figuring out their transit options.\n\n***\n\n### ☀️ 
 Weather & Expectations\n\nThis walk takes place in typical Toronto weather
  conditions. Please dress appropriately for the forecast and wear comforta
 ble walking shoes.\nThe route includes a mix of paved streets\, trails\, a
 nd potentially uneven or unpaved surfaces. There will be some distance to 
 cover\, so this walk is best suited to people who are comfortable walking 
 for around three hours\, with breaks.\n\nThis is a social walk\, not a rac
 e. We’ll keep a steady pace and make time to enjoy the surroundings.\n\n
 🌦️ **This event happens rain or shine!**\n\n***\n\n### 🧢 Meetup De
 tails\n\n📍 **Starting Location:** Outside the Dollar Tree near Kennedy 
 Station\n🫎 **Look for me wearing my Moose Hat!**\n⏰ **Meetup Time:** 
 11:00 AM\nI will only wait 5 minutes.\n**Early is on time. On time is late
 .**\n🏁 **End Point:** Shops at Don Mills\, North York\n🚇 **Transit:*
 * We’ll finish near the Eglinton line. I’ll help anyone who needs dire
 ctions for getting home by transit.\n\n***\n\n### 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**
 $5 cash in person or e-transfer to [mathewmaclean@hotmail.com](mailto:math
 ewmaclean@hotmail.com)**\nThis fee helps support the group and allows us t
 o continue organizing walks and other events throughout Toronto.\n\n***\n\
 n### ☕ After the Walk\n\nOnce we reach Shops at Don Mills\, anyone who w
 ants to continue the outing can join us for coffee\, pastries\, or a bite 
 to eat.\nIt's a chance to relax\, chat\, and get to know one another after
  our walk. Participation is optional.\n\n***\n\n### 🎒 What to Bring\n\n
 💧 Water\n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n🥨 A snack\n🧥 Weather-app
 ropriate clothing\n📱 Your phone or camera for photos\n\n***\n\n### 🌈
  Who Is This For?\n\nThis walk is great for:\n\n* People who enjoy discove
 ring hidden parts of Toronto\n* Anyone interested in local history and unu
 sual landmarks\n* Walkers who enjoy exploring trails and ravines\n* People
  looking to meet others and make friends\n* Anyone who wants to spend a fe
 w hours outdoors enjoying the fall colours\n\nThe trails and Rainbow Tunne
 l are part of the adventure\, but **the people you meet along the way are 
 the real experience.**\n\n***\n\n**REMEMBER:** You're welcome to RSVP ahea
 d of time or just show up on the day if you're unsure about your schedule.
 \nSometimes things happen and events may need to be cancelled or changed\,
  so please keep an eye on the event page for updates.\n\n👤 **Organizer:
  Mathew**\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or email **[torontomoviesando
 utings@hotmail.com](mailto:torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com)**\n\n**Com
 e for the trails.**\n**Stay for the conversation.**\n**Leave with a new co
 nnection — and maybe a new friend.** 🍂💛
