SUMMARY:Sunday Afternoon Movie Trivia and Great Memories!
DESCRIPTION:Try New Things in Toronto!\nHello everyone\,\n\nJoin us for a 
 fun and relaxing Sunday afternoon celebrating some of the greatest movies 
 ever made!\n\nWe'll revisit unforgettable movie scenes\, famous quotes\, m
 emorable characters\, and classic films from across the decades. Enjoy som
 e friendly trivia\, laughter\, conversation\, and great memories while mee
 ting new people.\n\nWhether you're a movie enthusiast or simply enjoy a li
 ttle nostalgia\, everyone is welcome!\n\nPlease note that we are at The Ph
 easant: A Firkin Pub at 1999 Avenue Road (roughly 6 blocks north of Lawren
 ce and south of the 401). We are in the back dining area—come find us!\n
 Joined by my other groups too :)\n\nEvent details below:\n\nSincerely\,\n\
 nSteve Flemming\n(Organizer/Host)\nSoul City Social Club\n\n***\n\n## EVEN
 T DETAILS\n\n**Event:** **Sunday Afternoon Movie Trivia and Great Memories
 !**\n**Date:** Sunday\, November 8\, 2026\n**Arrival Time:** 3:00 pm to 3:
 45 pm\n**Location:** The Pheasant: A Firkin Pub\n1999 Avenue Road\, Toront
 o\n**Hosted by:** Steve Flemming — Soul City Social Club\n**Age requirem
 ent:** 19+\n**Event fee:** $10 per person for reserved seating and event o
 rganization.\nFood and drinks are purchased separately.\n\n***\n\n## FRIEN
 DLY REMINDERS\n\n* Please mention Steve with Meetup when you arrive.\n* Pa
 y the event fee in cash at the event or by e-transfer in advance to: [stev
 eflemming11@gmail.com](mailto:steveflemming11@gmail.com)\n* Great lunch an
 d dinner menu and food specials available.\n* One beverage or appetizer mi
 nimum upon arrival to support the venue.\n\n***\n\n## PARKING AND TRANSPOR
 TATION\n\nFree street parking is available in the surrounding residential 
 neighbourhood.\n\nThe Pheasant is located on Avenue Road\, north of Lawren
 ce Avenue and south of Highway 401.\n\nFor those taking public transportat
 ion\, it's approximately a 15–20-minute walk from Yonge and Lawrence.\n\
 nLooking forward to an enjoyable afternoon of movie trivia\, wonderful mem
 ories\, and good company!
