SUMMARY:🍁 Fall Walk: Glen Stewart Ravine & Beach Boardwalk Adventure! 
 🍦🌊
DESCRIPTION:Try New Things in Toronto!\n## 🍁 **Fall Walk: Glen Stewart 
 Ravine & Beach Boardwalk Adventure!** 🍦🌊\n\nJoin us for a **beautifu
 l fall walk** through one of Toronto’s most scenic spots — the **Glen 
 Stewart Ravine** — followed by a stroll along the **Beach Boardwalk**!\n
 \nWe’ll take in the crisp autumn air\, the colourful leaves\, and the so
 und of the waves — plus a treat (or two) along the way.\n\nOur walk begi
 ns at **Main Subway Station**\, where we’ll make our way down **Main Str
 eet**\, head east along **Kingston Road**\, and then wander through the **
 Glen Stewart Ravine** — one of Toronto’s best hidden gems.\nAfter expl
 oring the ravine\, we’ll stop for a well-deserved treat at **Ed’s Real
  Scoop**\, home to some of the *best ice cream in the city*! 🍨\nIf you
 ’re not in an ice cream mood\, no worries — there’s a cozy coffee sh
 op right across the street. ☕\n\nFrom there\, we’ll head down to the *
 *Boardwalk**\, walk along the lake\, loop around **Ashbridges Bay** and fi
 nish our adventure at **Woodbine Beach**\, taking in those gorgeous fall v
 iews of the water.\n\nThis is the perfect way to soak up the fall season b
 efore winter sneaks in! 🍂\n\n**A Special Guest Joining Us!**\n\nWe're e
 xcited to welcome Miles Howard\, visiting us from Boston on November 14–
 15!\n\nMiles is writing *HIKE EVERY CITY*\, a book (coming in 2028) explor
 ing urban hiking\, community\, and how exploring cities on foot brings peo
 ple together. He also runs a similar urban hiking project in Boston called
  *Walking City Trails*.\n\nHe'll be joining us for both weekend outings\, 
 including this walk\, to experience our group firsthand and meet our membe
 rs.\n\nFeel free to say hello\, share your experiences\, and chat with Mil
 es if you'd like. No pressure\, of course!\n\nIt's exciting to see our com
 munity getting noticed beyond Toronto. Let's give Miles a warm welcome!\n\
 n***\n\n### 📍 **Meetup Details**\n\n**Meeting Spot:** Outside **Main Su
 bway Station** — I’ll be waiting and easy to spot in my **Moose Hat!**
  🦌\n**Meeting Time:** **11:30 A.M.** (I’ll wait about 5 minutes befor
 e we head out.)\n**Ending Spot:** **Woodbine Beach**\n\n***\n\n### 💲 **
 Meetup Fee**\n\n$5 (cash 💵 or e-transfer 📲 to **mathewmaclean@hotmai
 l.com**)\nYou can send it before or the day of the event!\n\n***\n\n### 
 🥾 **What to Bring**\n\n* Water\n* Comfortable walking shoes\n* A snack 
 or a few bucks for ice cream ☺️\n* A cozy sweater — it might get bre
 ezy by the water!\n\n***\n\n### 💬 **Stay Connected**\n\n👉 📱 **Don
 ’t forget to join our WhatsApp group** – [CLICK HERE!](https://chat.wh
 atsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc?mode=ac_t)\nGet updates\, event reminder
 s\, and chat with other friendly walkers!\n\n***\n\n### ⚠️ **A Quick N
 ote**\n\nSometimes things come up and I might need to cancel or reschedule
 . Please keep an eye on the event page for updates.\n\n***\n\n### 👋 **A
 bout This Group**\n\nThis group is open to **everyone** — whether you’
 re single or not\, new to Toronto\, or just looking to be social and make 
 friends!\nWe also host **movies\, hikes\, arts & culture events\, and rest
 aurant outings.**\nYou can RSVP ahead of time — or just show up the day 
 of if you’re feeling spontaneous!\n\n***\n\n**Organizer:** Mathew\n📧 
 **torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com**\n\n**Come for the fall colours.**\
 n**Stay for the friendship.** 🍁💛
